    "Line I: orange, very steep positive slope (~3), y-intercept ~2, arrowheads both ends, Roman numeral 'I' near its top",
    "Line II: light blue, shallow positive slope (~0.5), y-intercept 3, Roman numeral 'II' near its top right",
    "Line III: teal, moderately steep positive slope (~2), y-intercept -3, Roman numeral 'III' near its top right",
    "Line IV: dark blue, negative slope (~-2), y-intercept 3, Roman numeral 'IV' near its lower right",
    "candidate line (dashed purple) controlled by the slope and intercept sliders, pivoting about its y-intercept",
    "rise-over-run marker (right triangle with 'rise' and 'run' labels) shown on the clicked line",
    "y-intercept highlight dot on the clicked or candidate line"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "slopeSlider",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Slope m",
      "range": [-4, 4, 0.25],
      "default": 1,
      "teaches": "Slope controls direction and steepness: positive m rises left to right, negative m falls, and larger |m| means a steeper line — rotating the candidate line shows which Roman-numeral line a given m could match"
    },
    {
      "id": "interceptSlider",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "y-intercept b",
      "range": [-5, 5, 0.5],
      "default": 1,
      "teaches": "The y-intercept slides the whole line up or down without changing its tilt, and it is what distinguishes lines with the same direction — e.g. lines II and IV both cross at y = 3 while line III crosses at y = -3"
    },
    {
      "id": "selectLine",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Clicking a labeled line reveals its rise-over-run triangle and y-intercept, connecting its visual steepness and crossing point to concrete values of m and b that an equation must have to match it"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Read the four lines",
      "narration": "Four lines share the plane: I, II, and III rise left to right (positive slope) while IV falls (negative slope). Line II is the shallowest, line I the steepest.",
