Build an interactive figure using Chart.js.

CONCEPT: A linear equation y = mx + b is fully determined by its slope m (direction and steepness) and y-intercept b (where it crosses the y-axis), and matching an equation to one of four graphed lines means reading off exactly those two numbers.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Two numbers completely pin down a line: b tells you where it crosses the y-axis and m tells you its direction and steepness — so matching an equation to a graphed line is just reading those two features off the picture.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

